	(text "SOFT START (C2 = Css)\nC2 feeds back VOUT to GATE through D3, so VOUT ramps at a fixed rate:\n  dV/dt ~ [(VIN - Vp)/R2 - Vp/R1] / C2,  Vp ~ 2.5-3 V (DMP4025LSD plateau, check on scope)\n  Inrush ~ C_load x dV/dt.  Ramp time ~ VIN / (dV/dt).\nWith R2 47k, R1 100k, C2 220nF into 680 uF:\n  12 V: ~0.8 V/ms, ~15 ms, ~0.55 A    19 V: ~1.5 V/ms, ~13 ms, ~1.0 A\nC2 100nF = ~2x faster/higher inrush; 470nF = ~2x slower/lower.\nD3 blocks the Miller path at turn-off (fast off, ~1 ms); R4 resets C2 (~0.2 s)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 303.022 49.53 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "00e41cd0-d376-4632-b24c-7128be4eac8c")
	)
	(text "5 V PRE-REGULATOR"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 250.19 168.91 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "03fa99a8-6c7d-4421-8ff6-20b239568650")
	)
	(text "LAYOUT\nQ1: both drains (pins 5-8) carry full current - use copper pours.\nPins 1 and 3 (S1, S2) join on the PCB as VS.\nD2 close to Q1, short GND return. C2/D3/R4 close to Q1 pin 4."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 304.546 71.628 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "0a369c64-5810-4dd1-bbf1-c37d15804240")
	)
	(text "3.3 V ESP32 LDO"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 250.19 219.71 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "3a91b976-5c29-450b-801d-2d918cfac343")
	)
	(text "PROTECTION\nReverse input: Q1A body diode blocks; GATE ends up positive so both FETs stay off.\nD2 sits on VS, behind Q1A, so it never sees reverse polarity and F1 does not blow.\nSurge: Q1A body diode passes it to VS where D2 clamps (32.4 V at full pulse current).\nWrong adapter (> 22 V) will overload D2 and blow F1 - this circuit has no OV cut-off.\nQ1 VDS 40 V; VGS limited to 10 V by D1."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 302.768 32.258 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "3adb1ebd-a66e-493c-b8b5-94a4e8cb7e51")
	)
	(text "REVERSE-POLARITY PROTECTED, SOFT-START, SWITCHED DC INPUT"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 302.514 17.272 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "6296d29f-8e7a-4f95-9cd7-63e322577736")
	)
	(text "U3 retained: 3 A, 500 kHz forced PWM. 0.6 x (1 + 100k/16k2) = 4.304 V.\nL1 6u8: ripple ~0.93 A p-p at 16 V, nominal 500 kHz. Local ceramics at VIN/SW.\nC45 10u / 50V X5R: ~3u typical at 16V; estimated VIN ripple ~0.13Vpp at 1A output.\nFeeds both 3.3 V LDOs. Do not substitute the PFM LMR51430X version.\nVIN_SENSE is advisory: mute/shut down early during a falling input; verify hold-up on bench."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 250.19 203.2 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "b40fd449-2b08-454a-8c41-97a55ebe8d49")
	)
	(text "19 V max in (SMBJ20A). Q1 = DMP4025LSD dual P-FET: unit A blocks reverse input, unit B is the switch.\nClose J2 (or bridge JP1) to turn on: R2 pulls GATE low, both FETs turn on, D1 limits |VGS| to 10 V.\nSwitch current < 0.5 mA. Open: R1 pulls GATE to VS and both FETs turn off."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 302.514 23.622 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "ebfb2e4a-4b41-4a74-8dd9-0830129e5279")
	)
	(text "TLV1117LV33: 1 A; tab = output. Retained topology, reduced input voltage.\nAt 0.25 A: ~0.25 W; at 0.5 A: ~0.50 W; at 1 A: ~1.00 W.\nUse copper heat spreading. C52 10u ceramic plus C55 22u at ESP32.\nTPS7A2033 on DAC sheet supplies only the DAC."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 250.19 224.79 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "ed135f35-e03f-493a-9671-cef7feff26a6")
	)
